    "knowledge_point": "Adding Square Matrices",
    "problem": "Calculate $A+B$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "We add the corresponding entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2+4 & 5+1 \\\\ 3+(-2) & 1+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
